The console sketch in this directory is built by packages/engine/scripts/esp32s3-arduino.sh. The built app and
its partition table are not kept in this repository. The script pins them by SHA-256 in
checks/console/netlist.json and files those bytes in the blob cache.

The sketch compiles with Arduino CLI 1.5.1 and the esp32:esp32 core 3.3.12. That core is not
kept here. Its package is LGPL-2.1-or-later. HWCDC and the HAL files it builds with are
Apache-2.0. The prebuilt libraries under esp32s3-libs are ESP-IDF's, under the terms named in
packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/NOTICE. The script checks the SHA-256 of that core's
esp32s3-libs/3.3.12/qio_qspi/include/sdkconfig.h and installs nothing.

The knob sketch is built by the same script. It links LVGL 9.3.0. LVGL is under the MIT
License, reproduced with its notice in packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-lvgl. LVGL's memory
allocator is the TLSF allocator, under packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-tlsf, and its printf is
Marco Paland's, under the MIT License reproduced with its notice in
packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-printf. The cubic-bezier routine of LVGL's src/misc/lv_math.c
comes from the bezier-easing project, under the MIT License reproduced with its notice in
packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-bezier-easing. The image holds LVGL's Montserrat fonts at 14,
28 and 48 px. Their Montserrat glyphs are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, reproduced
with the Montserrat Project Authors' notice in packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-montserrat, and
their symbol glyphs come from Font Awesome Free 5, whose fonts are under the same licence,
reproduced with the Fonticons, Inc. notice in packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/LICENSE-fontawesome.
The caller names the LVGL tree. The script checks that tree's hash and copies nothing of it
into this repository.

libraries/knobpanel is a QSPI IO and an ST77916 panel after Espressif's esp_lcd_st77916,
which is under the Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2023-2024 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO
LTD. The build includes packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/screen/main/vendor_init.inc beside the port.
That file holds the panel maker's init sequence.
